# Locales (lt, en, et, lv, ja, zh)

- **Canonical:** `en/index.html`, `js/library.js` → then `npm run generate:et-lv`
- **Manual:** `lt/` HTML, `ja/`, `zh/`, all privacy pages (`lt/privatumas.html`, `*/privacy.html`)
- **ZH:** `html lang` / `hreflang` = `zh-Hans`; folder and `data-lang` stay `zh`
- **Do not** hand-edit `et/` or `lv/` for EN parity — use the generator
- CI: no uncommitted diff in `et/index.html`, `lv/index.html`, `js/library.{et,lv,lt}.js`
- Locales are a wave, not a ceiling. N+1 = [MULTILINGUAL playbook](../../docs/MULTILINGUAL_STRUCTURE.md) §7 + one release. Strategy: [GLOBAL_EPIC.md](../../docs/GLOBAL_EPIC.md)
- Never 302 away from `/{locale}/` (IP or Accept-Language). Switcher / nudge: [locale-switcher](../skills/locale-switcher/SKILL.md)

Details: [docs/MULTILINGUAL_STRUCTURE.md](../../docs/MULTILINGUAL_STRUCTURE.md)
